    excerpt: "Google's March 2026 update targets AI-generated content. Here's what changed and what it means for creators who use AI responsibly.",
    content: `<h2>The Problem</h2><p>For the past year, the internet has been flooded with AI-generated content. Blogs that write themselves, "articles" with no original insight, content that exists purely to game search rankings.</p><p>Google noticed. Users noticed. And Google just did something about it.</p><h2>What Changed</h2><p>The March 2026 update specifically targets: thin AI content, content with no original insight, content that exists solely for SEO manipulation, and sites that produce content at inhuman scale without evident human oversight.</p><p>The message is clear: Google wants content that's actually useful, not content that's just keyword-stuffed.</p><h2>What This Means for You</h2><p>If you're using AI to generate actual content — writing articles, creating posts, generating ideas — you're fine. Google's not targeting AI usage. They're targeting low-quality content regardless of how it was created.</p><p>The sites getting penalized are the ones producing thousands of articles per day with no human involvement. If you're writing 3-5 quality pieces per week with AI assistance, you're in the clear.</p><h2>How to Stay Safe</h2><p><strong>Add original insight.</strong> Don't just summarize what others have said. Bring your own perspective, experience, and opinion.</p><p><strong>Human editing.</strong> Every piece of AI-assisted content should go through human review. Fix errors, add nuance, inject personality.</p><p><strong>Don't chase volume.</strong> 5 great posts beat 500 generic ones every time.</p><p><strong>Be transparent.</strong> If you're using AI, say so. Trust is a competitive advantage.</p><h2>The Irony</h2><p>Google's crackdown on AI content actually benefits quality creators. All those low-quality sites that were crowding out real content? They're going away. The vacuum they're leaving behind is being filled by creators like you — people who actually have something to say.</p><p>That's the opportunity. Be the voice that cuts through the noise.</p><p><strong>Rating: 8/10</strong> — Finally, quality over quantity. This update is good for real creators.</p>`,
